## Short answer: Almost correct, but two bugs.

---

## Bug 1 — `vis` and `onPath` type mismatch

You declared them as `vector<bool>` in `findOrder` but `vector<int>` in `dfs` parameters:

```cpp
// findOrder declares:
vector<bool> vis(numCourses, false);
vector<bool> onPath(numCourses, false);

// dfs expects:
bool dfs(int i, vector<int>& vis, vector<int>& onPath, ...)
```

This will cause a **compile error**. Fix — make both consistent:
```cpp
vector<int> vis(numCourses, 0);
vector<int> onPath(numCourses, 0);
```

---

## Bug 2 — Cycle detected but you still return partial answer

When a cycle is detected, `dfs` returns `true`, but `findOrder` ignores that return value and still returns whatever is in `ans`:

```cpp
for(int i = 0; i < numCourses; i++){
    if(!vis[i]){
        dfs(i, vis, onPath, adj, s, ans);  // return value ignored!
    }
}
```

The problem says return `{}` if cycle exists. Fix:

```cpp
for(int i = 0; i < numCourses; i++){
    if(!vis[i]){
        if(dfs(i, vis, onPath, adj, s, ans)){
            return {};  // cycle detected
        }
    }
}
```

