## 7. Child using exec() to run a different program
```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>

int main() {
    pid_t pid = fork();

    if (pid == 0) {
        printf("Child (PID: %d) replacing itself with 'ls' command\n", getpid());
        // Child replaces its entire process image with 'ls'
        execlp("ls", "ls", "-l", NULL);
        // This line only runs if exec fails
        printf("exec failed!\n");
        exit(1);
    } else {
        printf("Parent (PID: %d) waiting for child to finish ls\n", getpid());
        wait(NULL);
        printf("Parent done\n");
    }
    return 0;
}
```
**Key concept:** `exec()` **replaces** the child process with a completely different program (`ls` here) — child's code after `execlp` never runs.

